# Godot 4 Project Rules

## Core Principles
- Use GDScript for game logic (primary language for Godot)
- Follow Godot's node-based architecture patterns
- Use signals for communication between nodes
- Prefer composition over inheritance

## Scene Structure
- Create modular scenes: GameManager, LocationManager, NPCSpawner, UI components
- Use Main scene as orchestrator, individual location scenes as subscenes
- Keep NPC as independent scene with its own logic and state machine
- Use CanvasLayer for UI elements (health bar, location selector)

## Code Organization
- Use PascalCase for class names and node names
- Use snake_case for variables, functions, and file names
- Group related functionality in autoload singletons (GameState, NPCManager)
- Keep scene scripts focused on that scene's responsibility

## Performance Considerations
- Use object pooling for NPCs (don't constantly instantiate/free)
- Implement viewport culling - only update visible location
- Use Area2D for NPC boundary detection rather than constant position checks
- Cache frequently accessed nodes with @onready var

## Godot 4 Specific
- Use new syntax: @export, @onready, func _ready():
- Leverage new TileMap system for location backgrounds
- Use CharacterBody2D for NPCs with built-in collision
- Implement state machines using match statements or State pattern
